<title>GERMANY: ABB Germany Q1 sales up.</title>
<headline>ABB Germany Q1 sales up.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish-Swiss engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG's German unit posted a nine percent rise in sales during the first quarter to 1.5 billion marks ($870 million), chief executive Michael Pohr said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Incoming orders were up 21 percent on a year earlier at 2.4 billion marks, Pohr told Deutsche ABB's annual shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>Pohr reaffirmed a forecast he made in March that sales and earnings for the full year would be in line with 1996. Sales rose last year by five percent to 8.7 billion marks, while net profits fell to 121 million marks from 172 million.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.724 German Marks)</p>
